          Alberto Clerici
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  German philosopher George Hegel, 1821:
  "In England even the poorest of people believe they have Rights; this is 
very different from what satisfies the poor in other lands."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Frigid winter melted into fragrant spring.  Giovanna d'Arco marched on 
Chandrapur (#1801) with her forces.  Viewing the eastern horizon, one can 
see a Forest province known as Alderwood (#101).  It is said that Prometeo 
is the ruler there.  It is known to be populated by Dragons.  If need be, 
they can call on a host of Dragons to defend their territory.  To the north 
is a forbidding mass of ice which seemingly has no end.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to Giovanna d'Arco invaded the 
province of Chandrapur, a Plain area owned by the provincial garrison 
commander.  Giovanna d'Arco was in command of the attacking armies.  The 
defenders were commanded by the provincial garrison commander.  The armies 
were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Chandrapur (1801):

  185th   
  Lt Cav  
