  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 243rd Light Cavalry, the 215th Camel Corps, the 
331st Bowmen and the 332nd Bowmen in reserve.  Giovanna d'Arco marched with 
her loyal troops, eyes set in terrible determination.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of the acting commander.
  As luck would have it, Giovanna d'Arco's formations were well hidden by a 
sudden mist, giving them a small edge.  Further, in this perilous slugging 
match, Giovanna d'Arco seemed to have the tactical edge.
  The Elves led by Giovanna d'Arco were not impressed by her strange 
appearance.
  Across the whole front, the Elite 259th Legion were visited by a mighty 
Thunderbird who flew down from the stars to aid their Divine cause, and were 
inspired to fanaticism by its divine spectacle.  They faced the 197th Legion.
The 242nd Light Cavalry and the 185th Light Cavalry flanked the enemy and 
charged in with full strength.  The 259th Legion battled with the 197th 
Legion and lost no time in crushing their lines.
  Giovanna d'Arco's great horde overpowered the army of the acting commander 
and took the field, dispersing their enemies.  The 259th Legion annihilated 
the 197th Legion.
  Giovanna d'Arco's host ended the campaign victoriously and conquered the 
province of Chandrapur.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we 
could not have been better satisfied with the elan of the 243rd 
Light Cavalry, and we have raised its ranking to Veteran.
  During early summer, Giovanna d'Arco moved into Jaguardo (#1701) with her 
army.
  With the advent of the late summer season Giovanna d'Arco was tutored in 
White Magic by Drake.  Giovanna d'Arco practiced for months and her skill in 
White Magic increased.
  All characters of this high level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.

  With the advent of the fall season, Giovanna d'Arco tried a Bless spell, 
but botched it.  Her experience improved her prowess in White Magic.
  Congratulations!  You have attained level 6 in White Magic.  Your 
characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The White Magician can now use the magic of 
certain Holy Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  At 
any Monastery, Altar or Great Hall, the success chance to cast a White Magic 
spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied 
when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is 
applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, and 
is not occupied by a monster.

  With the coming of the early winter season Bairn was resurrected by the 
spell cast by Giovanna d'Arco.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Giovanna d'Arco for this year.


  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Giovanna d'Arco 
treated with her ally Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with 
her ally Hokuto (#4).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Prometeo (#5).  
Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Kahn (#6).  Giovanna d'Arco treated 
with her ally Circe (#8).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Agesilao 
(#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  The 182nd Trolls was hired by a local count of Pearlgate to subdue a 
rebellious baron and rose to Average quality.


  Here is the financial report for Giovanna d'Arco's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 59 gold in revenue.  14 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 54th Garrison and the 55th Garrison trained well and improved 
in quality.  42 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Giovanna d'Arco 
was left with 28 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Rolando
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I enlisted the 54th Garrison and the 55th Garrison in Cascadia 
to serve the provincial garrison commander.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I worked hard on my Tactics 
but was frustrated in my efforts.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  I tried to 
improve my Tactics, but the task was beyond my aptitude.
  With the coming of the fall season, I moved into Moussoro (#1604) with my 
high-spirited army.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I marched on Milo's Crossroads 
(#1504) with my command.  To the west there is a Plain province known as 
Mammoth (#1404), a land of no races where Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
reigns.

  Thy humble servant,   Rolando


From: Hakim
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I roamed around in Sageleaf, exploring the terrain there, and 
now 100% of it has been explored.  I discovered also that Sageleaf has been 
the site of terrible battles.  Many intrepid warriors have perished on its 
soil: the 176th Legion (Veteran Humans).  In my travels, I saw no marauding 
monsters.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I journeyed to Jaguardo.  In 
my travels, I encountered no monsters.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  I moved into 
Tigerhome.  While adventuring, I encountered no wandering monsters.
  In fall, I travelled about Tigerhome, exploring its features.  After my 
exploration efforts, 60% of it has been explored to date.  In my travels, I 
saw no wandering monster.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I explored Tigerhome well and 
now 90% of it has been explored.  I found a feature in Tigerhome: a Cavern 
(#23) inhabited by the Black Dragon.  Legend says the Sword Excalibur is 
hidden here.  The Black Dragon is an Evil and very powerful acid-spitting 
dragon.  While adventuring, I encountered no wandering monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Hakim


From: Tiffany
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Bless spell.  Milo's Crossroads was magically blessed 
and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 171st Phalanx were Blessed and 
permanently destroyed.  My efforts raised my aptitude in White Magic.
  Windy spring was followed by a sultry early summer.  I tried to practice 
my White Magic, but the task was beyond my ability.  My efforts improved my 
aptitude in White Magic.
  With the advent of the late summer season I really tried hard to improve 
my White Magic, but I practiced in vain.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into fall.  I was instructed in Psychic 
Magic by Isis.  I practiced my Psychic Magic and improved noticeably.
  During early winter, I tried to practice my Element Magic, but the task 
was beyond my aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Tiffany


From: Moosu, Squire to Drake
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Drake set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He journeyed to Sageleaf.  He also found a Cave (#102) in 
Sageleaf, occupied by the Marilith Demon.  What treasure may lie there is 
unknown.  The Marilith Demon is a very powerful 6-armed female demon with 
the tail of a giant snake.  Each arm is capable of skillfully wielding a 
weapon.  While adventuring, Drake saw no wandering monster.
  In early summer, Drake travelled to Jaguardo.  He encountered no monster.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Drake practiced his White Magic 
diligently for many weeks, but could make no significant progress.
  The summer surrendered to a colorful fall.  Drake searched throughout 
Jaguardo for Bairn.  Drake encountered Bairn.  Drake waved his hands and 
gestured rhythmically, meaning to cast a Spiritwrack spell, but it backfired 
and a dove popped out of his hat instead.  Weaving his artful words of magic 
into a mighty Mirror-Image Phantasm spell, Bairn gestured with his hands and 
an image of Drake sprang into existence!  Drake disbelieved the illusion of 
Drake and it faded away.  Drake chanted his strange words of magic and cast 
a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist in the shape of a cross formed around 
Drake.  By Drake's special Advanced White Magic powers, the spell caused 
Bairn to shriek in pain and inflicted 10 damage points.  Bairn dropped to 
the ground, mortally pierced.  And so it came to pass that Bairn met his 
tragic end.
  The fall season darkened into the stillness of early winter.  Drake cast a 
Bless spell.  Tigerhome was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless 
affected no armies in Tigerhome.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Drake


From: Isis
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to sweet spring, and I made ready to carry out my urgent 
assignments.  I rode into Pearlgate.  While adventuring, I saw no marauding 
monsters.
  During early summer, I was tutored in White Magic by Tiffany.  I practiced 
well and improved my skill in White Magic.
  With the coming of the late summer season I was tutored in the art of 
White Magic by Tiffany.  I practiced for many weeks and my skill in White 
Magic increased.
  The summer surrendered to a colorful fall.  I practiced my Psychic Magic 
diligently for many weeks, but could make no significant headway.
  During early winter, I was tutored in Element Magic by Tiffany.  I 
practiced my Element Magic and my skill in Element Magic went up.

  Thy humble servant,   Isis


